        <body>
            <div xml:id="d359">

                <pb facs="0436" n="324" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg324"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.51/301</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Cuban Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">De
                        Céspedes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 63</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 29, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: Your excellency is aware
                    that the negotiations for a loan to Cuba by the Treasury of the United States
                    were successfully terminated yesterday.</p>
                <p>In my Government’s name I have the honor of thanking your excellency for the
                    interest that you have taken in this matter, as also your distinguished
                    colleague the Honorable Secretary of the Treasury and all the officials of the
                    two Departments with whom this loan has been conducted.</p>
                <p>May I ask you to be good enough as to express to them, at the same time, my
                    personal appreciation of courteousness and attentions?</p>
                <p>With the assurances [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Carlos Manuel de Céspedes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d359-a1.xml" xpointer="d359-a1"/>
            </div>
